  "review_scope": [
    "First completed certifying point stage and exact operation ordering, all finite stages, signed transition neighbours, ties, stationary origin and terminal refusal semantics.",
    "Actual source origins for dynamic and paused/resumed prescribed rotation, force-error history separation, split and pre-split impulse semantics.",
    "Immutable owner-authenticated namespaced cache entries on the original bounded LRU and original work/ledger; original charge/callback/deadline policies.",
    "Request-private entry receipt before public/helper dispatch; raw descriptor resolution and absence witnesses; exact native function/global identity checks.",
    "Direct recording source traversal through the normal .22 point selector; old recording cursor remains unused.",
    "Original C3 six controls and 38 physical observations; no claim of universal legacy/.22 equality.",
    "Independent source reader selector replay and original expected values; parent/reader own their full source/reference/numerical gate receipts."
  ],
  "explicit_limits": [
    "Private immutable receipt tuples, owner tables, request-local closure code/cells and native error construction remain trusted implementation metadata. No general Python-interpreter sandbox is claimed.",
    "Native FunctionType globals/closure/builtins/class pointers are read-only on the three actual tested CPython versions; their mutable dictionaries/keyword contents still receive current identity/content checks.",
